    "narrative": "The Austin Waves project a balanced attack today, though **Gunnar Henderson** stands out as the premier play with an elite score of 70.72. Facing Kevin Gausman, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a 14% boost due to his dynamic platoon advantage against RHP, coupled with Gausman\u2019s notoriously slow delivery, which creates an optimal environment for **Gunnar Henderson** to exploit the stolen base category. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (64.86) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (63.63) are high-ceiling anchors today; both benefit from strong platoon splits against Michael Soroka and Huascar Brazob\u00e1n respectively. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains a focal point as well (64.55), as the projected park factors and his intrinsic power profile against Shane Baz overcome a slight negative adjustment for platoon dynamics.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup optimizer today was the exclusion of **Nasim Nunez**, who finished with a 46.44 score. While **Nasim Nunez** provides high-end speed potential, his projected spot at the bottom of the order (-6% penalty) pushed him just below the threshold required to displace the high-floor production of **Dominic Smith** or **Andy Pages**. The current starting lineup prioritizes the consistency of **Sam Antonacci**, whose 56.83 score is bolstered by a favorable 0.376 xwOBA and a prime leadoff spot against Aaron Nola. \n\nManagers should keep a close eye on the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters, particularly **Liam Hicks**, as any drop in order position would necessitate a re-evaluation of his 44.71 efficiency score. Additionally, while **Kyle Tucker** carries an impressive 64.36, he faces Jos\u00e9 Soriano, whose ability to limit baserunners could suppress the ceiling of our middle-of-the-order bats like **Andy Pages**. We are essentially betting on our core of **Gunnar Henderson**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** to create enough traffic to offset the risks posed by elite arms like Nola and Gausman.",
